ort_curvature&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&ref=sha256%3A9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5%2Fnodes%2Fsupport.full_relative_support_curvature","record":{"assumption_ids":["scalar.paper_minimizer"],"boundary":"Ordinary authored deduction checked against retained mathematical inputs; no new Lean declaration, elaborated dependency, cross-model transport, Comparator acceptance or independent proof certification is asserted.","citation_ids":["authored_r8_support_full_relative_support_curvature","authored_r10_empty_support_chord"],"evidence_ids":["ordinary_deductions_review_20261026","ordinary_r10_proof_route_review_20261026"],"id":"support.full_relative_support_curvature","kind":"claim","label":"Full support by contact and local curvature","locator":"Long reasoning record #qualitative-terminal-gap","source_id":"authored_long_comparisons_20261024","statement":"For an admissible pure zero-field SK minimizer, its Stieltjes support is [0,1). A finite-chord comparison using q(0)=0, q<=1 and strict zero-interval convexity excludes empty support; contact and positive-plateau curvature exclude bounded gaps; zero-plateau curvature excludes an initial gap. At a last support point r, the terminal chord obstruction gives q(t)<t and G(r)<0, contradicting atom addition. Consequently q(t)=t and E[Phi_xx(t,X_t)^2]=1 for 0<=t<1. This alternate proof does not use the quantitative terminal defect estimate.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.full_relative_support_curvature","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.full_relative_support_curvature","id":"field:79ab724ec039319142d3aa040482db4cdd1d72647c9c6724d83238024243eaef","kind":"assumption_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb